{"id": "unknown-2026-10-01-011", "date": "2026-10-01", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 40, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "U.S. small-scale solar adds 1.6 GW in Q2", "content": "<p>Distributed solar maintained a steady deployment pace alongside 2.5 GWh of new behind the meter storage, even as a wave of thermal generation additions pulled solar's total share of new US power capacity down to 55%.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/01/u-s-small-scale-solar-adds-1-6-gw-in-q2-2026-as-fossil-fuel-capacity-surges/\">U.S. small-scale solar adds 1.6 GW in Q2</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p>\n", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/01/u-s-small-scale-solar-adds-1-6-gw-in-q2-2026-as-fossil-fuel-capacity-surges/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-01-012", "date": "2026-10-01", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 40, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "South Korea grid overhaul to connect more than 100 GW of renewables", "content": "<p>South Korea plans to replace hard limits on grid connections with curtailable access, battery storage, and competitive allocation of connection rights, as it aims to accommodate more than 100 GW of renewable energy capacity by 2030.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/01/south-korea-grid-overhaul-to-connect-more-than-100-gw-of-renewables/\">South Korea grid overhaul to connect more than 100 GW of renewables</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/01/south-korea-grid-overhaul-to-connect-more-than-100-gw-of-renewables/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-01-013", "date": "2026-10-01", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 40, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Two-stage pyrolysis process turns waste solar panels into silicon carbide", "content": "<p>Russian scientists have developed a process that combines pyrolysis at 500 C with electric arc treatment above 1,800 C. The resulting solid product contained up to 61% silicon carbide, a material used in power electronics and refractory ceramics.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/01/two-stage-pyrolysis-process-turns-waste-solar-panels-into-silicon-carbide/\">Two-stage pyrolysis process turns waste solar panels into silicon carbide</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/01/two-stage-pyrolysis-process-turns-waste-solar-panels-into-silicon-carbide/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-01-014", "date": "2026-10-01", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 40, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Spanish researchers validate 10,000 cycles for iron-lead flow battery", "content": "<p>A Spanish-developed iron-lead flow battery uses a single electrolyte loop and a fluorine-free membrane to cut costs and reliance on critical raw materials, with kilowatt-scale modules the next development step. </p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/01/spanish-researchers-validate-10000-cycles-for-iron-lead-flow-battery/\">Spanish researchers validate 10,000 cycles for iron-lead flow battery</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/01/spanish-researchers-validate-10000-cycles-for-iron-lead-flow-battery/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-01-015", "date": "2026-10-01", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 40, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Ireland energizes first SRESS solar farm, opening new revenue opportunities for farmers and landowners", "content": "<p>\"This is the beginning of a wave of small-scale energy projects being developed by farmers and communities,\" Ken O'Byrne, of Flogas Energy told <b>pv magazine</b>. Flogas has a 15-year PPA with the 650 kW Meadhill Solar farm's developer, Cork farmer Sean Keating. </p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/01/ireland-energizes-first-sress-solar-farm-opening-new-revenue-opportunities-for-farmers-and-landowners/\">Ireland energizes first SRESS solar farm, opening new revenue op", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/01/ireland-energizes-first-sress-solar-farm-opening-new-revenue-opportunities-for-farmers-and-landowners/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-01-016", "date": "2026-10-01", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 40, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Indian PV manufacturer Vishakha Renewables files for IPO", "content": "<p>Vishakha Renewables, jointly promoted by the Vishakha Group and the Adani Group, produces four of the six key components used in solar modules and is the largest solar component manufacturer (non-cell) in India in terms of combined installed production capacity as of March 31, 2026. </p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/01/adani-group-backed-vishakha-renewables-files-for-ipo/\">Indian PV manufacturer Vishakha Renewables files for IPO</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/01/adani-group-backed-vishakha-renewables-files-for-ipo/", "type": "rss"}]}
